---
description: Code quality, security, and forbidden patterns
alwaysApply: true
---

# Code Quality

- Keep functions small and reusable
- Add comments only for non-obvious logic
- Prefer clarity over cleverness

# Security

- Validate all user input (Zod on the server)
- Never trust client-side data
- Use Supabase RLS policies for row-level access control
- No hardcoded secrets — use environment variables

# Forbidden

- ❌ Direct DB queries in UI components
- ❌ Large logic blocks inside API handlers
- ❌ Hardcoded secrets or credentials
